Subject: [PATCH 689/689] docs: qualify sustained VHI preview performance

---
 .acd/decisions/20261021-vhi-camera.md | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/.acd/decisions/20261021-vhi-camera.md b/.acd/decisions/20261021-vhi-camera.md
index c91967a527..5df080a17c 100644
--- a/.acd/decisions/20261021-vhi-camera.md
+++ b/.acd/decisions/20261021-vhi-camera.md
@@ -25,7 +25,9 @@ The final driver uses a persistent task producer, MJPEG decode through
 jfif.library and aligned packet slots that avoid split-TRB short-length errors.
 Five combined video/microphone sessions and four stop/reopen cycles pass;
 removing the camera returns NotFoundError. Preview frame rate remains below the
-requested 5 fps (typically 2-4 fps in these bounded sessions). No Twitch or
+requested 5 fps (typically 2-4 fps in these bounded sessions). A longer restored
+run delivered 175 displayed frames in 226 seconds while both tracks stayed
+live, so sustained preview performance remains a limitation. No Twitch or
 bare-metal claim is made. Website/playback release regressions are recorded
 separately from capture proof.
 
